  "extracted_items": {
    "callouts": [
      {
        "type": "abstract",
        "title": "Purpose",
        "body": "This scaffold guides the [[Elaborative-Interrogation|self-explanation]] process for passages requiring the deepest processing — dense theoretical arguments, multi-step mechanisms, complex distinctions. Use it during the [[Performance-Phase]] when your Forethought process goals specify self-explanation at section boundaries. Based on [[Chi-et-al.|Chi et al.'s (1994)]] self-explanation research: self-explanation forces integration of new information with [[Prior-Knowledge|prior knowledge]], which is the mechanism that produces genuine understanding rather than surface familiarity. See [[The-Fluency-Illusion]].",
        "line_number": 24,
        "source": "SRL-Self-Explanation-Scaffold.md",
        "char_start": 565,
        "char_end": 1205
      },
      {
        "type": "tip",
        "title": "When to Use",
        "body": "- Dense theoretical sections where you notice comprehension slipping\n- Multi-step mechanism descriptions where causal chains are complex\n- Sections containing key distinctions that require precise understanding\n- Any passage flagged in your Forethought Protocol as requiring deep processing\n- When you catch yourself re-reading without generating new understanding",
        "line_number": 27,
        "source": "SRL-Self-Explanation-Scaffold.md",
        "char_start": 1206,
        "char_end": 1602
      },
      {
        "type": "warning",
        "title": "This IS the comprehension test.",
        "body": "If you cannot explain this section to a skeptical colleague in two sentences, you have not yet understood it. The inability to compress is diagnostic of incomplete processing. See [[The-Generativity-Diagnostic]].",
        "line_number": 122,
        "source": "SRL-Self-Explanation-Scaffold.md",
        "char_start": 3731,
        "char_end": 3991
      },
      {
        "type": "tip",
        "title": "After Completing This Scaffold",
        "body": "- If you completed it fluently → the section is well-understood; move on\n- If you struggled at Steps 2 or 7 → flag this section for Cold Reconstruction in Self-Reflection\n- If you couldn't complete Step 4 → your understanding may be surface-level; re-read with attention to the author's reasoning, not just their conclusions\n- If Step 5 produced rich connections → this is the material for permanent note creation",
        "line_number": 143,
        "source": "SRL-Self-Explanation-Scaffold.md",
        "char_start": 4508,
        "char_end": 4970
      },
      {
        "type": "connections-and-links",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "- [[Elaborative-Interrogation]] — The self-explanation process this scaffold implements\n- [[Chi-et-al.]] — The foundational research demonstrating the self-explanation effect\n- [[The-Fluency-Illusion]] — Why passive re-reading feels productive but isn't\n- [[The-Generativity-Diagnostic]] — The compression test operationalizes generativity\n- [[Deep-Processing]] — Self-explanation activates deep (not shallow) processing\n- [[Transfer-of-Learning]] — Step 8 tests for genuine understanding via transfer\n- [[Metacognitive-Monitoring]] — Struggle detection during scaffolding is monitoring",
        "line_number": 151,
        "source": "SRL-Self-Explanation-Scaffold.md",
        "char_start": 4976,
        "char_end": 5604
      }
    ],
